    {
      "id": "9be79304-f031-446e-9175-41a669829bd5",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -96,
        96
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 608,
        "content": "## Out of Office - Emergency Client Router\n### How it works\n\n1. Monitors Gmail for incoming messages.\n2. Extracts content and uses Gemini to analyze urgency.\n3. Routes emails based on classification results.\n4. Notifies the team on Slack for urgent items.\n5. Logs data to Google Sheets and sends auto-replies.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure Gmail credentials for the inbox trigger.\n- Set up Google Gemini API keys in the HTTP Request node.\n- Connect Slack integration for team notifications.\n- Set up Google Sheets for escalation logging.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the Gemini prompt to change classification criteria or update the Slack channel ID for different teams."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b59c1bcb-30ca-4930-964a-8a594cba728d",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        464,
        176
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 640,
        "height": 304,
        "content": "## Watch inbox and extract fields\n\nWatches the Gmail inbox and sets up initial variables and email fields for processing."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5cbb8704-3385-4fd6-ac3d-bdbbe711374d",
